{
  "name": "Ex02b Stage 2 — The IF Node",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "manual",
      "name": "Run Workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [240, 400],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "input",
      "name": "Set Mood",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [440, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            { "id": "i1", "name": "mood", "value": "happy", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "gate",
      "name": "Is happy?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [640, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": { "caseSensitive": true, "leftValue": "", "typeValidation": "strict", "version": 2 },
          "conditions": [
            { "id": "g1", "leftValue": "={{ $json.mood }}", "rightValue": "happy", "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "equals" } }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "happy",
      "name": "Happy Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [880, 280],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            { "id": "h1", "name": "message", "value": "Glad you're feeling happy. Keep it up!", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sad",
      "name": "Sad Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [880, 520],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            { "id": "s1", "name": "message", "value": "Cheer up. Things will get better.", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-goal",
      "name": "Stage 2 — The IF node and binary routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 60],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 200,
        "color": 7,
        "content": "## Stage 2 — The IF node and binary routing\n\nFive nodes. The IF compares the upstream `mood` field against the literal `\"happy\"` and routes to one of two branches.\n\n**What this stage drills:**\n- The IF node — left value, right value, operator. The `options.version: 2` field is required (n8n quirk).\n- *Binary routing*: an IF node has TWO outputs. Top output = true branch. Bottom = false branch.\n- *Two terminal nodes*: each branch ends at a different Set node. Which one runs depends on the IF's decision.\n- *Try both paths*: change `mood` in *Set Mood* to anything other than `happy` and re-run. Watch the false branch fire instead."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-test",
      "name": "Test both branches",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [880, 700],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 360,
        "height": 160,
        "color": 4,
        "content": "## Don't trust an IF you've only run once\n\nA workflow with an IF that you've only tested in one direction is half-tested. Always run with each input that exercises a different branch.\n\nFor this stage: run with `mood: happy`, then change to `mood: sad` (or anything else), run again."
      }
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Run Workflow": { "main": [[{ "node": "Set Mood", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]] },
    "Set Mood": { "main": [[{ "node": "Is happy?", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]] },
    "Is happy?": {
      "main": [
        [{ "node": "Happy Response", "type": "main", "index": 0 }],
        [{ "node": "Sad Response", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": { "executionOrder": "v1", "timezone": "Asia/Singapore" }
}
